Its grammar is derived from the ShExC grammar (section 6) of the specification "Shape
Expressions Language 2.1", Final Community Group Report, 8 October 2019, edited by Eric
Prud'hommeaux, Iovka Boneva, Jose Emilio Labra Gayo and Gregg Kellogg, by the Contributors to
the Shape Expressions Language 2.1 Specification, published by the W3C Shape Expressions
Community Group under the W3C Community Contributor License Agreement (CLA),
https://shex.io/shex-semantics-20191008/. This attribution is the one section 2.2 of the CLA
asks of derivative works. spec/shex-2.1.ebnf is extracted from the specification;
spec/deviations.ebnf changes some of its productions; gen/ebnf2lezer.mjs generates
shex.grammar, the parser built from it and words.ts from both.

The productions numbered with the suffix "s" and "t" in spec/shex-2.1.ebnf restate
productions of SPARQL 1.1 Query Language (https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-sparql11-query-20130321/)
and RDF 1.1 Turtle (https://www.w3.org/TR/2014/REC-turtle-20140225/), W3C Recommendations
